  "story": {
    "enabled": true,
    "heading": "The Story",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Jordan Rakei was born in New Zealand, raised in Brisbane, Australia, and is now based in London. His music moves between neo-soul, jazz and electronic production, built around his falsetto-leaning voice.",
      "Wallflower (2017) was shortlisted for the Australian Music Prize; What We Call Life (2021) and The Loop (2024, his first release on Decca) continued a catalog defined by close collaboration with jazz and soul musicians.",
      "In 2024, Rakei was named the first-ever Artist in Residence at London's Abbey Road Studios."
    ]
